Thanks all, for the tips.  Next time I'll know not to ::ahem:: kill
the priest in minetown just because he's cross-aligned, work harder to
cavort with foocubi I encounter along the way, and preserve potions of
smoke, levitation, and enlightenment.

This time, having failed to do all those things, I just took a bunch
of wands of wishing, my limited ability with my dig spell, and a lot
of patience, and completely cleared the structure from level 20 of my
dungeon, where I proceeded to invoke the PYEC on my bag of tricks
about 18 times to farm potions of gain level, wraiths, and whatever
else I could get.  This worked quite well.

After going through all three altars on the Astral plane and finding
no co-aligned altar, I got cornered by Death and lost 180 of my 370 HP
cap before it occurred to me that I needed to move away from him more
than I needed to kill him.  Went back to the first altar, which was
thankfully co-aligned (I either misread the first time or something
very strange was going on), and Traeki the Tourist, at long last,
walked to the heavens to stand at the feet of the Lady herself.

Woohoo!

That's Wizard, Archaeologist, and Tourist down.  Healer next.  If I
pull that off, I'll have to try for some kind of conduct challenge.

Any recommendations for a compellingly tricky, but fairly accessible,
conduct?  I might also just try to ascend one of each class, first,
but ascending a Valkyrie or Barbarian at this point sounds...sort of
